as the president prepares for his speech  there are long lines at testing sites  all across the country right now as  americans prepare for the holidays and  of course this is the second holiday  season in a row  under a major coveted threat so for more  on all of it let's bring in dr celine  gander an epidemiologist at nyu and  bellevue hospital here in new york city  she was also on the biden harris covett  transition team and she joins us from  kansas city this morning dr gander good  morning to you thank you for coming back  to us since we have the president's  speech later today i am curious from a  public health perspective what do you  want to hear from him  so one i really want to hear a focus on  hospitalizations and deaths we are  seeing hospitalizations skyrocket  deaths on the rise in parts of the  country where people are not vaccinated  and i think that really needs to come  through that there is a very real impact  of vaccination on risk of ending up in  the hospital of risk of of  uh secondly i i'm very interested in  hearing more about his plans to make  rapid testing much more available to the  american public as we've heard  uh they will be opening up a website  similar to what has been done in the uk  where you can log on and order free  rapid tests to be delivered to your home  and i think that's really going to make  a big difference for a lot of people in  managing their risk  when it comes to rapid tests how  accurate are they what do we know about  how reliable they're going to be since  they're going to be going out in great  numbers in the days and weeks ahead  this is a very good question and i think  one way to think about rapid tests is if  the result is positive you have coded if  it's negative and you have symptoms you  may still want to get a pcr they do  sometimes miss uh that diagnosis  especially early in the course of  disease uh so again positive rapid  engine test you have covet if it's  negative and you think you had a high  risk exposure you have symptoms still go  get a pcr  okay now when we were taking these  vaccinations we were told this will give  us optimal protection um now we're  seeing a rise in breakthrough cases with  those that are vaccinated what do you  attribute to this  well i think the cdc over promised  honestly i think we had some really  exciting data back in the spring  very soon shortly after vaccination you  do have this brief honeymoon period  where you are very unlikely to get any  infection but what we know is that that  level of protection wanes what's left  over after that is protection against  severe disease hospitalization and death  and those are really the outcomes to be  focused on here the other issue is  omicron is relatively immune evading and  so while the vaccines offer very good  protection against severe disease  hospitalization and death with omicron  you are going to see breakthrough  infections with omicron so if you really  do want to protect yourself for whatever  reason against any infection you need to  layer other interventions like masking  and all the rest  so four days before christmas a lot of  people planning heading to the airport  you think it's wise to travel right now  when they're in the middle  people feel like we're back to march  2020.  well look what i'm trying yesterday  from new york city to kansas city  my husband and i had an early lunch so  that we wouldn't have to eat on the  plane or  in the airport  we wore n95s in the car with the windows  open on the way to the airport at 95's  on the plane the entire flight uh and  then uh some of the other things we've  done we've gotten rapid tests the entire  family is going to be rapid testing  every day uh i got my sister uh you  could call it a bit of a lump of coal i  got her  three hepa air filtration units to put  in the living room dining room  kitchen  you know i think that's smart dr  gallander i i like a sister like that i  don't think that's a lump of call at all  to keep the family safe  god exactly exactly so we're going to  stay safe but we're still going to  celebrate together  so we keep hearing conflicting things  about how reliable the home tests are  and detecting the omicron variant can  you tell us anything can you shed any  light on that  yeah there have been some um  discrepancies in results particularly in  some of the sports leagues and broadway  theaters where they're testing every day  with multiple different kinds of tests  so if you have  a discordance between test results uh  you know where one is positive one is  negative you see that um evolving over  in real time in in settings like that  because they're testing so much  um what i would say again is the tests  are probably by and large still useful  and reliable  but if you have a negative test result  on a rapid test and you've had a high  risk exposure somebody you know  had coveted or you have symptoms i would  still go get a pcr test  uh you know at your local public health  department  another place for example in new york  city that's been great is our health and  hospital system by far  much more efficient and fast than lining  up at some of the urgent cares so i  would really reach out to your local  public health department and see what's  the best place to get a pcr if your  rapid antigen test is negative  all right dr gaunder and i think that's  good advice get your sister or your  relative a hepa filter  merry christmas  thank you  thank you so much
 

